      "content": "{\"base_revision\": \"sha256:0f99aff3bf9f4c24e80707b49f1e91dd84a240ac54151686fa22c836d980b65c\", \"decision\": \"revise\", \"issues\": [\"visible_rail_continuity: The VCC net has an excessive detour from J1 to U1 pin 8, crossing the R1/C2 area unnecessarily. This violates the 'easy to follow' visual rubric for power rails.\", \"label_association: Field owner association is weak for C2 and R2; their labels are geometrically closer to neighboring components (U1, R1) than their own symbols in some metrics, though within limits. The layout feels cluttered in the top-left quadrant.\"], \"actions\": [{\"operation\": \"add_wire_path\", \"net\": \"VCC\", \"from_ref\": \"J1\", \"from_pin\": \"1\", \"to_ref\": \"U1\", \"to_pin\": \"8\", \"waypoints\": [{\"x_mm\": 48.26, \"y_mm\": 92.71}, {\"x_mm\": 54.61, \"y_mm\": 92.71}, {\"x_mm\": 54.61, \"y_mm\": 45.72}, {\"x_mm\": 78.74, \"y_mm\": 45.72}, {\"x_mm\": 78.74, \"y_mm\": 49.53}]}], \"rationale\": \"The current VCC path from J1 (Supply) to U1 pin 8 is routed via a long detour through the R1/C2 region. This creates visual clutter and obscures the direct connection between the power source and the IC supply pin. The proposed path uses orthogonal segments aligned to the 1.27mm grid, routing directly from J1 upwards, then right towards U1, avoiding unnecessary crossings of other nets or components. This improves readability and adheres to the visible_rail_continuity requirement for clear, unambiguous power distribution.\"}"
    },
